  "result": "The sign-in decision is in `src/server/services/session-service.ts`. `createSessionToken` sets `SESSION_TTL_DAYS = 30` and computes `expiresAt` from it. The login and register actions (`src/actions/auth/login.ts`, `src/actions/auth/register.ts`) call that function and pass the expiry to `setSessionCookie`.\n\nThe later-request check is in `src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts`. `findSessionByTokenHash` loads the row by hashed token and returns `null` when `row.session.expiresAt <= new Date().toISOString()`. That is the point where an expired session stops resolving.\n\n`src/lib/session.ts` also re-checks `expiresAt` against `Date.now()` in `getSessionPrincipal`, but that is a second guard on the same expiry, not a separate decision. I left it out of the answer.\n\nANSWER: src/server/services/session-service.ts, src/server/repositories/session-repository.ts",
